ments to see if the service is running.\n\nSo the next logical step is to use the exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd tool to get the list of pods and deployments in the social-network namespace. This will help verify if the user-service pod is actually running or if there are any deployment issues. By checking the pods, they can see if there are any crashes or restarts, and look at the deployment status to ensure the correct number of replicas are running. If the user-service isn\'t listed, that\'s a clear sign of a problem. If it is listed but in a crash loop, that points to a different issue. This step is crucial to confirm the current state of the service before diving deeper into metrics or traces.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \n"kubectl get pods -n social-network"  \nTo verify if the user-service pod is running, I need to check the current state of pods in the social-network namespace. This will confirm whether the service is deployed and operational, or if there are issues like crashes, restarts, or deployment failures. This is a critical first step to validate the service\'s existence and health before further investigation.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 387, 'prompt_tokens': 1661, 'total_tokens': 2048, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd10-6e1d-7053-b031-99d476fc76ad-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1661, 'output_tokens': 387, 'total_tokens': 2048}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='8aa69530-eac1-4606-94bf-326dae9eca99'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose a problem in their social network application, which is made up of many microservices. They mentioned that some or none of the microservices might have faults. The goal is to identify the faulty components and their root causes.\n\nFirst, the assistant started by using the `get_services` tool to list all services in Grafana. That makes sense because knowing which services are present is the first step. Then, they tried to check the metrics for the user-service using `get_metrics` with a PromQL query. The response came back empty, which might indicate that the user-service isn't running or isn't being monitored properly.\n\nNext, the assistant used `exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd` to run `kubectl get pods -n social-network` to check the pods in the social-network namespace. The response from the tool call wasn't shown, but based on the previous step where the metrics were empty, it's possible that the user-service pod isn't running. If the pod isn't running, that could be the root cause of the issue.\n\nNow, the user is in the thinking stage again. The assistant needs to decide on the next tool. Since the previous steps didn't find the user-service pod, maybe they should check the deployments or replica sets for that service. Using `kubectl get deployments` or `kubectl get replicasets` could show if there's a deployment issue, like zero replicas or deployment failures. Alternatively, checking the logs with `kubectl logs` might provide more insight into why the pod isn't running. Another possibility is to look into the service's configuration to ensure it's correctly set up and that there are no network issues preventing it from starting. The assistant should consider these steps to dig deeper into why the user-service isn't functioning as expected.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get deployments -n social-network"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9ffc581423208e96', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 402, 'prompt_tokens': 2652, 'total_tokens': 3054, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd10-7fb4-7820-b9df-1bc6bdd86e29-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get deployments -n social-network'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9ffc581423208e96', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2652, 'output_tokens': 402, 'total_tokens': 3054}), ToolMessage(content='NAME                     READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE   AGE\ncompose-post-service     1/1     1            1           117s\ncustom-service           0/3     3            0           35s\nhome-timeline-redis      1/1     1            1           117s\nhome-timeline-service    1/1     1            1           117s\njaeger                   1/1     1            1           117s\nmedia-frontend           1/1     1            1           117s\nmedia-memcached          1/1     1            1           117s\nmedia-mongodb            1/1     1            1           117s\nmedia-service            1/1     1            1           117s\nnginx-thrift             1/1     1            1           117s\npost-storage-memcached   1/1     1            1           117s\npost-storage-mongodb     1/1     1            1           117s\npost-storage-service     1/1     1            1           117s\nsocial-graph-mongodb     1/1     1            1           117s\nsocial-graph-redis       1/1     1            1           117s\nsocial-graph-service     1/1     1            1           117s\ntext-service             1/1     1            1           117s\nunique-id-service        1/1     1            1           117s\nurl-shorten-memcached    1/1     1            1           117s\nurl-shorten-mongodb      1/1     1            1           117s\nurl-shorten-service      1/1     1            1           117s\nuser-memcached           1/1     1            1           117s\nuser-mention-service     1/1     1            1           117s\nuser-mongodb             1/1     1            1           117s\nuser-service             1/1     1            1           117s\nuser-timeline-mongodb    1/1     1            1           117s\nuser-timeline-redis      1/1     1            1           117s\nuser-timeline-service    1/1     1            1           117s\n', id='8e44b06c-45b4-48ed-915c-b95b675609aa', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-9ffc581423208e96'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='d3e817a3-482b-4c4d-bba0-25dbf2ee1ba4')]]
