haps the init container is named "hang-init". I should check the logs of that init container instead. Using kubectl logs on the pod with the init container\'s name might work. Let me try that.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \n"kubectl logs custom-service-5cb49889f5-dw62n -n social-network --previous -c hang-init"  \nThe error indicates the init container might be named "hang-init". Retrieving its logs will clarify why the initialization phase is failing, as init containers often handle setup tasks like volume mounting or pre-start checks that could block the main container from starting.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=190, prompt_tokens=3986, total_tokens=4176, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd10-dc33-77b3-a8da-6a04418b9627-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3986, 'output_tokens': 190, 'total_tokens': 4176}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='6425c47a-026c-4f60-a3b7-e95eaa006703')]]
