is information, I cannot proceed with effective rollback operations.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 960, 'prompt_tokens': 621, 'total_tokens': 1581, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd13-a886-7ea1-80ba-523b68329a03-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 621, 'output_tokens': 960, 'total_tokens': 1581}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='263f703a-5286-4287-9837-d33f37118a53'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, so the user wants me to generate a tool call based on the previously chosen tool, which was get_previous_rollbackable_cmd. Let me think about how to approach this.\n\nFirst, the tool name is get_previous_rollbackable_cmd, and its description says it\'s used to retrieve a list of commands that can be rolled back. The parameters for this tool are empty, as indicated by the parameters section in the tool definition. That means I don\'t need to provide any arguments when calling it. \n\nWait, the user\'s previous step was to choose the get_previous_rollbackable_cmd tool, and now they want the tool call. Since the parameters are empty, the tool call should just be the name of the tool with an empty arguments object. \n\nLet me double-check the tool\'s parameters. The parameters section in the tool definition shows "properties": {} and "type": "object", so there are no required arguments. Therefore, the correct tool call is {"name": "get_previous_rollbackable_cmd", "arguments": {}}. \n\nI need to make sure there\'s no mistake here. Sometimes, even if the description says no parameters, maybe there\'s an implicit argument. But according to the tool\'s definition, 